# DEVFLOW-FIX-BASE-REF-1 — Canonical Remote Base Resolution

Durable doc: `docs/architecture` n/a · runbook
`docs/runbooks/devflow-canonical-base-resolution-runbook.md` · sprint doc
`docs/sprints/devflow-fix-base-ref-1-canonical-remote-base-resolution.md`.

## Permanent rules (DEVFLOW-R011..R020)

1. **Exact SHA is the comparison authority.** Every DEVFLOW diff/scope/manifest
   conclusion is computed against an exact commit SHA. A base branch **name** is
   discovery authority only.
2. **The canonical remote outranks the local ref.** With no authoritative exact
   SHA supplied, the base comes from the configured remote-tracking ref after a
   fetch. A stale / ahead / diverged local branch never changes a result.
3. **No silent fallback.** Never `refs/heads/<base>`, `main`, `master`, `HEAD`,
   `HEAD~1`, or the latest tag. Remote or authority failure **fails closed** with
   an actionable error — never a governance PASS.
4. **Exact SHAs are validated as commits.** Must match the exact-object-id
   pattern (40/64 hex) *and* resolve to an existing commit object. Revision
   expressions (`HEAD`, `HEAD~1`, `ref^{}`), options, abbreviations, trees,
   blobs and unpeeled tags are rejected.
5. **Base is pinned per invocation.** Once resolved it is fixed for that run; a
   remote branch advancing afterwards cannot change it. A new invocation may
   resolve a newer base.
6. **Authority is reported.** Tools emit `BASE_SOURCE`, `BASE_BRANCH`,
   `BASE_SHA`, `HEAD_SHA` (+ `MERGE_BASE_SHA`, `LOCAL_BASE_STALE` when known).
   Never print a base branch without its exact SHA.
7. **Right checkout only.** Verify the repository root before comparing. A tool
   must never silently analyse a different worktree or the primary checkout
   (`BASE_WRONG_REPOSITORY`).
8. **CI prefers the immutable event base.** PR runs classify against
   `github.event.pull_request.base.sha`, not the moving `origin/<base_ref>`.
9. **Explicit canonical remote.** Named in config; never auto-selected. With
   `origin` *and* `upstream` present, guessing is forbidden — fail closed.
10. **Refs never become options.** Validate against an allowlist, pass as git
    argument-array operands, use `--` on `git diff`. Never interpolate a ref into
    a shell string.

## Semantics per consumer

| Need | Use |
|---|---|
| "changes introduced since the branch point" | `merge-base(BASE_SHA, HEAD)` |
| "difference against the exact base tip" | `BASE_SHA` |

Compute merge-base **from the pinned canonical SHA** — never replace
domain-correct merge-base semantics with a raw two-dot range just for
consistency. Consistency is about *authority*, not identical range syntax.

## Where the base branch name comes from

Single source of truth: `config('devflow.manifest.required_base_branch')`.
Do not duplicate the branch name into a new authority. `.sprint/current.yml`
declares it per sprint and the manifest validator compares the two.

## Implementation shape

* `App\Support\Devflow\CanonicalBaseRefResolver` — the only place a base is
  resolved. Do not add ad-hoc `git diff` / `merge-base` calls elsewhere.
* `App\Support\Devflow\CanonicalBaseRef` — immutable pinned result + output
  contract (`toKeyValueLines()`, `toArray()`).
* `GitChangeInspector` consumes the resolver; it never reads a branch name.
* `scripts/ci/resolve-gates.sh` validates and pins before diffing; any
  uncertainty resolves to `unknown_high_risk` (strongest gate).

## Gotchas

* **`git rev-parse -- <rev>` is wrong.** For `rev-parse`, `--` starts *paths*, so
  it asks about a file named `<rev>` and always fails. Validation — not `--` —
  blocks option injection there. `git diff` *does* take a trailing `--`.
* An unresolved base must surface as **unresolved**, not as an empty change set:
  an empty set passes every contradiction check and silently fakes a GO.
* CICD-CTRL-1 invariant is untouched: `docs_only` stays the only
  critical-skipping profile; the default profile stays `unknown_high_risk`.

## Verify

```bash
php artisan devflow:base-ref-check --strict
php artisan foundation:devflow-check --strict     # DEVFLOW-BASE-AUTHORITY
php artisan sprint:manifest-check
php artisan sprint:scope-audit
php artisan test --filter='DevflowCanonicalBaseRef|CiClassifierBaseAuthority'
```

## Out of scope

This sprint changes governance tooling only. It authorizes **no** clinical,
billing, lab, inventory, SATUSEHAT, branch-isolation or Legacy-RME behaviour
change, and no deploy/rollback/backup contract change. Historical GO tags remain
immutable.
